  "summary": {
    "derivative_id": "der:rc4:cb_d44bbd714bbc48daa9e1b734fb404cea:summary",
    "text": "The Russian Imperial Order of Saint Michael Archangel is a dynastic order that operates an Australian Division with a registered location in Victoria. It collects membership contributions\u2014identified on its site as a Foundation Contribution, an Annual Oblation and branch collections\u2014to fund the Order's running costs and to support \u2018humanitarian activities\u2019 and charitable works designated by Her Imperial Highness through the Australian Division Office. Branches may keep funds for local operating expenses and local charity support, with 25% of branch collections remitted to the Australian Division Office. The organisation maintains governance documents and an Australian Division office, and holds investiture ceremonies that include an Orthodox moleben (liturgical service). It offers membership sign-up and public investiture services."
  },
